.TH WT 1 "2026-10-02" "sc-fleet 0.1.0" "sc-fleet manual"
.SH NAME
wt \- one worktree per topic, every checkout a sibling, PRs on any forge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wt init
[\fB\-\-migrate\fR] [\fB\-\-mine\fR] [\fB\-y\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR \fIslug\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-clone\fR \fIurl\fR | \fB\-\-new\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-\-remote\fR \fIurl\fR | \fB\-\-forge\fR forgejo|github \fB\-\-org\fR \fIorg\fR]]
.br
.B wt new
\fIslug\fR [\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIp\fR] [\fB\-\-track\fR \fIremote-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR \fIref\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIname\fR]
.br
.B wt ls
[\fB\-a\fR] [\fB\-\-pr\fR] [\fB\-\-porcelain\fR]
.br
.B wt path
[\fIquery\fR]
.br
.B wt cd
[\fIquery\fR]   (zsh wrapper)
.br
.B wt sync
.br
.B wt pr
[\fB\-t\fR \fItitle\fR] [\fB\-b\fR \fIbody-file\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR \fIbranch\fR] [\fB\-\-draft\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-squash\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.br
.B wt rm
\fIslug\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B wt doctor
[\fB\-a\fR]
.br
.B wt help
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wt
runs the branch workflow for several projects, each with several topics in
flight, on a machine whose local disk need not be durable. Every checkout of a
repo is a sibling directory: the clone lives at
.IR src/<repo>/main
and each topic is a linked git worktree beside it, named by slug. Notes,
per-repo conventions and topic logs live in a durable store
.RI ( <store>/<proj>/ ,
by default
.IR ~/notes/projects/<proj>/ )
and are symlinked into the project directory. The same tool is called by a
human from a shell and by an agent such as Claude Code from a slash command,
so the procedure is deterministic and lives in one place.
.SH LAYOUT
.nf
<root>/<proj>/                         plain dir \(em never a git repo
\(bu CLAUDE.md -> <store>/<proj>/CLAUDE.md
\(bu docs      -> <store>/<proj>/
\(bu src/<repo>/
     main/                             the clone; stays on the default branch
       .claude/settings.local.json     repo-scoped allows (allow_interp=true only)
     <slug>/                           worktree, branch = <prefix><slug>
       CLAUDE.local.md -> docs/topics/<slug>.md   (git-excluded)

<store>/<proj>/                        durable store \(em git, pushed
\(bu CLAUDE.md  README.md
\(bu repos/<repo>.conf                 per-repo conventions
\(bu topics/<slug>.md  topics/archive/
.fi
.PP
.I $(git-common-dir)/info/exclude
carries
.B CLAUDE.local.md
and
.BR .claude/ ,
so nothing personal is visible to
.B git status
in a shared repo. Sibling repos of one project sit beside each other under
.IR src/ .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS wt init
Bootstrap or retrofit a project. Creates the wrapper and
.IR src/ ,
the store with stub
.B README.md
and
.BR CLAUDE.md ,
both symlinks,
.I repos/<repo>.conf
with inferred values (base = upstream when that remote exists; prefix = the
most common
.I dir/
prefix among remote branches whose tip you authored; forge from the base URL
host), the exclude entries, and
.B core.hooksPath scripts/hooks
when the repo ships hooks. Idempotent.
.TP
.BI \-\-project " slug"
Operate on
.I $WT_ROOT/slug
instead of the project derived from the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-clone " url"
Clone into
.IR src/<basename>/main .
With
.B \-\-project
this creates the project from nothing; inside an existing wrapper it adds a
sibling repo.
.TP
.BI \-\-new " name"
.B git init \-b main
at
.I src/name/main
with an empty root commit. Add
.BI \-\-remote " url"
to set origin and push, or
.B \-\-forge forgejo \-\-org
.I org
(creates the repo through the Forgejo API; needs the token) or
.B \-\-forge github \-\-org
.I org
(uses
.BR "gh repo create" ).
With neither, prints the remote-add line to run once the repo exists.
.TP
.B \-\-migrate
Move an old-layout clone at
.I src/<repo>
to
.IR src/<repo>/main .
Refuses when the clone is dirty or already has linked worktrees.
.TP
.B \-\-mine
Write interpreter allows
.RB ( "Bash(python3 *)" ", " "Bash(python *)" ", " "Bash(pytest *)" ", " "Bash(ruff *)" )
into
.I main/.claude/settings.local.json
and set
.B allow_interp=true
in the conf. For repos you own; never for someone else's checkout.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Reserved for future prompts; accepted and ignored today.
.SS wt new
Create a topic. Fetches the base remote, resolves its default branch, creates
branch
.I <prefix><slug>
from
.I base/<default>
(never from the local checkout), adds the worktree at
.IR src/<repo>/<slug> ,
seeds
.I docs/topics/<slug>.md
and links it into the worktree as
.BR CLAUDE.local.md .
The last line of output is the worktree path.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " p"
Override the conf prefix for this call
.RB ( "wt new \-\-prefix ll/fix/ widget" " \(-> " ll/fix/widget ).
.TP
.BI \-\-track " remote-branch"
Adopt an existing branch instead of creating one. The slug defaults to the last
path component.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " ref"
Branch from
.I ref
instead of the base default.
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " name"
Pick the repo when the wrapper holds several.
.PP
Refuses a slug containing
.BR / ,
the default branch name, an existing directory or branch, and a project whose
.I main
is missing. Warns when the project root
cannot hold a second copy of
.IR main/build* .
.SS wt ls
Table of worktrees: PROJECT REPO SLUG BRANCH \(+-BASE DIRTY NOTE [PR].
\(+-BASE is ahead/behind the repo's
.IR base/<default> ;
.B *
marks uncommitted changes; NOTE says whether a topic note exists.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Every project under
.IR $WT_ROOT ,
not just the current one.
.TP
.B \-\-pr
Ask the forge for the head's PR state
.RB ( "#6 open" ", " "#57 merged" ).
Network.
.TP
.B \-\-porcelain
Tab-separated
.IR "proj repo slug branch path" ,
no header, no colour, no art.
.SS wt path, wt cd
.B wt path
prints one worktree path: a unique substring match on
.I proj/repo/slug
or the branch name, otherwise an
.BR fzf (1)
picker when one is available on a terminal. The zsh function
.B wt cd
wraps it in a
.BR cd .
.SS wt sync
Inside a topic worktree: fetch the base remote and rebase onto its default
branch. On conflict it stops, lists the conflicting paths and leaves the rebase
in progress for
.B git rebase \-\-continue
or
.BR "git rebase \-\-abort" .
Refuses in
.I main
or on the default branch.
.SS wt pr
Land a topic: preflight (clean tree, not the default branch), sync, squash to
one commit unless the conf says
.B squash=false
or
.B \-\-no\-squash
is given (pre-squash subjects and bodies are carried into the commit body),
push (plain when fast-forward,
.B \-\-force\-with\-lease
when history was rewritten \(em the normal case after a squash), then open the
PR on the repo's forge and append a Log line to the topic note. An existing
open PR for the same head is reported, not duplicated.
.TP
.BI \-t " title"
PR and squash-commit title. Default: the HEAD subject.
.TP
.BI \-b " body-file"
PR body. Default: the note's Goal and Acceptance gate plus the commit list.
.TP
.BI \-\-base " branch"
A stacked PR: rebase onto and target
.I base/branch
instead of the default branch. The branch must already be on the base remote.
A branch created with
.B wt new \-\-from
records its parent in the topic note and takes it as the default base; a branch
that contains another pushed topic's commits without such a record is refused
until
.B \-\-base
names the parent, because squashing to the default branch's merge-base would
fold the parent topic into this PR. Squashing more than one commit requires
.BR \-t :
the last commit's subject is not a PR title.
.TP
.B \-\-draft
Draft PR (Forgejo: a
.B WIP:
title prefix).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-squash
Keep the commits for this call.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report ahead/behind, the squash plan, the forge and the commits; change nothing.
.SS wt rm
Remove a topic after its merge. Refuses when the worktree is dirty, has commits
not on its upstream (or never pushed), or the branch is not merged \(em merged
means an ancestor of
.I base/<default>
.B or
the forge reports the head's PR merged (a forge squash-merge rewrites the SHA,
so the ancestor test alone would refuse forever). Then
.BR "git worktree remove" ,
.BR "git branch \-D" ,
.B fetch \-\-prune
and the note moves to
.IR topics/archive/ .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Discard dirty or unpushed work and delete an unmerged branch. Never added by
Claude on its own.
.SS wt doctor
Per repo: layout, symlinks, conf, remote HEAD, exclude entries, forge
credential (token mode 0600 /
.B gh auth
/
.BR glab ),
free space on
.I $WT_ROOT
and stale worktrees.
.B \-a
covers every project.
.SS wt help
.B wt help
prints the synopsis;
.B wt help
.I command
opens this page at that command.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Site facts come from the fleet config,
.I ~/.config/sc-fleet/config
(and a per-machine
.I config.local
beside it, which wins), read with grep and never sourced; see
.BR sc (1)
.B config
to show the effective values.
.TP
.B notes
Notes root. Default
.IR ~/notes .
.TP
.B wt.root
Project root. Default
.IR ~/wt .
.TP
.B wt.store
Durable store root. Default
.IR <notes>/projects .
.TP
.BI wt.forge= "glob kind"
Repeatable. Maps a remote host glob to
.BR github ", " gitlab " or " forgejo ;
the first match wins, and
.I config.local
rules are tried before
.IR config 's.
Built in after them: github.com and
.B github-*
ssh aliases \(-> github, gitlab.com and
.B *gitlab*
\(-> gitlab, codeberg.org \(-> forgejo.
.TP
.B wt.forgejo_web
Forgejo base URL for
.BR "wt init \-\-new \-\-forge forgejo" .
Unset by default, and then that command refuses and names this key.
.TP
.B wt.token_file
Forgejo token file. Default
.IR ~/.config/forgejo/token .
.TP
.B wt.templates
Directory of text overlays. A
.I store-README.md
there replaces the built-in store README;
.BR {{PROJ}} ,
.B {{WRAP}}
and
.B {{STORE}}
are substituted.
.PP
Per repository:
.I <store>/<proj>/repos/<repo>.conf
\(em
.BR key=value ,
one per line,
.B #
comments allowed, parsed with grep and never sourced.
.TP
.B prefix
Prepended to the slug to form the branch, e.g. empty,
.B t/
or
.BR ab/feature/ .
.TP
.B base
Remote that holds the default branch:
.B origin
normally,
.B upstream
on a fork checkout.
.TP
.B push
Remote topics are pushed to. Default
.BR origin .
.TP
.B squash
.B true
(default) squashes in
.BR "wt pr" ;
.B false
keeps the commits.
.TP
.B forge
.BR auto ", " github ", " forgejo " or " gitlab .
.B auto
derives the kind from the base URL host through the
.B wt.forge
rules above.
.TP
.B allow_interp
.B true
writes interpreter allows into
.IR main/.claude/settings.local.json .
Default
.BR false .
.TP
.B web
Browser/API base
.RI ( https://<host> )
when the remote host is an IP or an ssh alias.
.SH FORGES
.TP
.B GitHub
.BR gh (1):
.BR "gh pr create \-\-base <default> \-\-head [fork-owner:]<branch>" ;
existing PRs via
.BR "gh pr list \-\-head" .
.TP
.B Forgejo
REST API with
.BR "Authorization: token <t>" :
.B GET /api/v1/repos/o/r
for the default branch,
.B GET .../pulls?state=open
filtered on
.BR head.ref ,
.B POST .../pulls
to create. Token from
.B $FORGEJO_TOKEN
or
.I ~/.config/forgejo/token
(mode 0600; created once in the web UI, Settings \(-> Applications, scope
.BR write:repository ).
Without a token
.B wt pr
pushes, prints the compare URL and writes the body to
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wt-pr-body.md .
.TP
.B GitLab
.BR glab (1):
.BR "glab mr create \-\-target\-branch <default> \-\-source\-branch <branch>" .
.SH WHAT CLAUDE READS
From a session started inside a worktree:
.I ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md
(user), the wrapper
.I CLAUDE.md
(ancestor directories load at launch; symlinks followed), the repo's own
.I CLAUDE.md
if any, and
.I CLAUDE.local.md
\(-> the topic note. Permissions come from
.IR main/.claude/settings.local.json ,
which Claude Code reads at the main checkout's root and applies to every
worktree; a shared
.I .claude/settings.json
in the wrapper would
.B not
apply (it loads from the launch cwd only). Auto-memory is one directory per
repository, shared by main and all worktrees.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WT_ROOT
Project root; overrides
.BR wt.root .
.TP
.B WT_STORE
Durable store root; overrides
.BR wt.store .
.TP
.B WT_TOKEN_FILE
Forgejo token file; overrides
.BR wt.token_file .
.TP
.B FORGEJO_TOKEN
Overrides the token file.
.TP
.B WT_FORGE_WEB
Forgejo base URL for
.BR "wt init \-\-new \-\-forge forgejo" ;
overrides
.BR wt.forgejo_web .
.TP
.B WT_TRACE
Non-empty enables
.B set \-x
(the debugger recipe).
.TP
.BR WT_NO_ART ", " NO_COLOR
Suppress the banners / the colours. Both are also off whenever stdout is not a
terminal, so scripts and Claude always get plain output.
.TP
.B WT_ART
Non-empty draws the banners even on a pipe.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I bin/wt
The tool, in the sc-fleet checkout; linked to
.I ~/.local/bin/wt
by
.BR install.sh .
.TP
.I ~/.config/sc-fleet/config
The fleet config (see CONFIGURATION).
.TP
.I tests/test_wt.sh
Offline suite against a
.B file://
origin:
.BR "bash tests/test_wt.sh" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a refusal or failure, with a
.B refuse
line on stderr saying why and what to do.
.SH EXAMPLES
Retrofit an existing clone, then run a topic end to end:
.nf
.RS
cd ~/wt/atlas && wt init \-\-migrate
wt doctor
wt new b3\-package && wt cd b3\-package
$EDITOR CLAUDE.local.md          # fill Goal and Acceptance gate
claude                           # sessions start inside the worktree
git commit ...                   # work
wt sync                          # main moved? rebase onto it
wt pr \-t "B3: package the simulator \(em self\-test"
cd .. && wt rm b3\-package       # after the merge
.RE
.fi
Create a project from an existing remote, or a brand-new repo of your own:
.nf
.RS
wt init \-\-project borealis \e
        \-\-clone forgejo@forge.example.org:acme/borealis.git
wt init \-\-project piste \-\-new piste \-\-mine \-\-forge forgejo \-\-org acme
.RE
.fi
Adopt a live remote branch with the repo's prefix already in its name:
.nf
.RS
cd ~/wt/atlas/src/atlas\-research
wt new \-\-track ab/feature/queue\-experiments
.RE
.fi
